===== Getting and Flashing Firmware =====


This board might come with a different firmware versions (MediaTek SDK, PandoraBox, Padavan, etc.). If your board comes with PandoraBox, you can install OpenWrt using sysupgrade. Just SSH to the router and perform forced
sysupgrade (due to a board name mismatch). The default IP of this board should be: 192.168.1.1 and username/password: root/admin. In case of a different firmware, you can use web based recovery described below.

Use the following command to perform the sysupgrade (for the 256MB RAM/16MB flash version):

<code>sysupgrade -n -F openwrt-ramips-mt7621-u7621-06-256M-16M-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin </code>


===== Flash via tftpd =====

  - Download firmware [[https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/19.07.7/targets/ramips/mt7621/]]
  - Change the file name from "//openwrt-18.....squashfs-sysupgrade.bin//" to "//root_uImage//" (without extension)
  - Connect your computer to the LAN1 router
  - Statically set your computer network card 10.10.10.3/24
  - Run Tftpd64, select network card 10.10.10.3 and select directory with "//root_uImage//" file
  - Press and hold the reset button
  - Input the power supply to the router
  - After about 30 seconds the router (10.10.10.123) will start downloading the firmware, which will be noticeable in the Tftp64 program
  - Release the reset button
  - Set the computer network card in DHCP mode
  - Expect to ping the device 192.168.1.1/24


